# Scripts and unit files that execute on Linux targets (routers, servers) must
# stay LF in the working tree even on Windows checkouts with core.autocrlf=true:
# busybox ash, procd and systemd cannot parse CRLF. These files also ship inside
# release tarballs built from a checkout (make package-openwrt normalizes too).
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.init    text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
Makefile  text eol=lf
# LuCI integration files ship in the router package too — and LuCI's template
# parser does NOT tolerate CRLF (a raw \r inside a write("...") literal is a
# Lua "unfinished string" error; field-found on iStoreOS 24.10).
*.lua     text eol=lf
*.htm     text eol=lf
# The example config ships in the router package; Go's YAML reader tolerates
# CRLF, but keep it LF like every other packaged file.
configs/config.example.yaml text eol=lf
